KG42.register("clusters-ca2e96a4b54ed3da3bd2d2d0",{"id":"42-data_center_space_time_flexibility::v142-d-K003","paper":"42-data_center_space_time_flexibility","label":"Multi-node allocation for a single flexible consumer and the equivalent hub virtual-link representation","record":{"cluster_id":"v142-d-K003","label":"Multi-node allocation for a single flexible consumer and the equivalent hub virtual-link representation","market_meaning":"A single flexible consumer submits the total requested quantity, the quoted price, and the delivery-node set; clearing determines the load at each node and charges according to the nodal price. Hub load, virtual load shifting, and hub price-difference remuneration are retained as an alternative representation of the same allocation and charging mechanism, and their equivalence is limited by unresolved index and domain conditions.","mechanism_ids":["v141-a-M02","v141-a-M03"],"market_types":["DEM"],"process_stages":["bidding","clearing","coordination","settlement"],"scope_disposition":"conditional","scope_explanation":"Both mechanisms are restricted to a single flexible consumer; cross-mechanism assembly is based on the source's explicit equivalence statement for (2.16) and (2.23), and cannot be extended to models with multiple consumers, with load-shifting cost, or with an independent computing-capacity constraint. The hub self-loop term is not yet closed.","assembly_status":"partial","boundary_rationale":"The two groups of chains jointly describe the rule by which the same consumer allocates load among selectable delivery nodes and bears the charges. The hub form is used to explain flexibility remuneration and is retained as an alternative representation; it is not counted separately as an independent rule.","chain_bindings":[{"chain_id":"v141-c-R006","ownership":"primary","role":"interface","rationale":"Provides the multi-node delivery demand declaration."},{"chain_id":"v141-c-R007","ownership":"primary","role":"core","rationale":"Gives the welfare clearing of the direct load decomposition."},{"chain_id":"v141-c-R008","ownership":"primary","role":"support","rationale":"Explains the clearing-price support for participant profit response."},{"chain_id":"v141-c-R009","ownership":"primary","role":"core","rationale":"Gives the per-node charge convention and the revenue reconciliation."},{"chain_id":"v141-c-R010","ownership":"primary","role":"alternative","rationale":"Retains the hub declaration representation of the same demand."},{"chain_id":"v141-c-R011","ownership":"primary","role":"alternative","rationale":"Retains the clearing candidate represented by total load and virtual load shifting."},{"chain_id":"v141-c-R012","ownership":"primary","role":"alternative","rationale":"Retains the equivalent profit representation of the hub charge and the price-difference remuneration."}],"connections":[{"connection_id":"v142-d-K003-J01","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R006","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R007","kind":"quantity_interface","from_refs":["v141-c-R006::theta::v141-c-R006-T001","v141-c-R006::theta::v141-c-R006-T002","v141-c-R006::theta::v141-c-R006-T003"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R007::theta::v141-c-R007-theta-bard","v141-c-R007::theta::v141-c-R007-theta-alphad","v141-c-R007::theta::v141-c-R007-theta-Nd"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e038","v141-b-g02-e009"],"rationale":"The same total quantity, quoted price, and delivery-node set enter the load-decomposition clearing."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-K003-J02","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R007","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R008","kind":"functional_coupling","from_refs":["v141-c-R007::phi::v141-c-R007-C001","v141-c-R007::phi::v141-c-R007-C002","v141-c-R007::phi::v141-c-R007-C003"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R008::phi::v141-c-R008-C002","v141-c-R008::phi::v141-c-R008-C003","v141-c-R008::phi::v141-c-R008-C004"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e009","v141-b-g02-e013","v141-b-g02-e014","v141-b-g02-e016"],"rationale":"The source explicitly maps the optimal prices and quotas of (2.16) to the profit problems of the consumer, the supplier, and the transmission network."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-K003-J03","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R008","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R009","kind":"quantity_interface","from_refs":["v141-c-R008::x::var_d_n","v141-c-R008::x::var_pi_n"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R009::x::v141-c-R009-X001","v141-c-R009::theta::v141-c-R009-T001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e010","v141-b-g02-e013","v141-b-g02-e015","v141-b-g02-e016"],"rationale":"The nodal load and nodal price in price coordination are used for per-node charging, and the price's roles as a variable and as a settlement parameter are retained."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-K003-J04","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R007","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R009","kind":"functional_coupling","from_refs":["v141-c-R007::phi::v141-c-R007-C003"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R009::phi::v141-c-R009-C002"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e009","v141-b-g02-e016"],"rationale":"The source links revenue adequacy to the balance constraints of the delivery node and the other nodes; the demand-notation conversion still must be checked."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-K003-J05","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R010","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R011","kind":"quantity_interface","from_refs":["v141-c-R010::theta::theta_bar_d","v141-c-R010::theta::theta_alpha_d","v141-c-R010::phi::v141-c-R010-C001"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R011::theta::v141-c-R011-T-bar-d","v141-c-R011::theta::v141-c-R011-T-alpha-d","v141-c-R011::phi::v141-c-R011-C003"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e019","v141-b-g02-e020"],"rationale":"The hub demand data and the alternative-node range bound the total cleared load and the shiftable range; the set parameters missing from R011 are not additionally constructed."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-K003-J06","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R011","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R012","kind":"quantity_interface","from_refs":["v141-c-R011::x::v141-c-R011-X-d","v141-c-R011::x::v141-c-R011-X-delta","v141-c-R011::theta::v141-c-R011-T-alpha-d"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R012::x::v141-c-R012-x-d","v141-c-R012::x::v141-c-R012-x-delta","v141-c-R012::theta::v141-c-R012-theta-alpha-d"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e019","v141-b-g02-e020","v141-b-g02-e024"],"rationale":"The hub cleared total load and the virtual load shift enter the profit and remuneration expressions; the self-loop index difference between the two chains remains unresolved."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-K003-J07","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R007","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R011","kind":"alternative_representation","from_refs":["v141-c-R007::x::v141-c-R007-x-dn","v141-c-R007::phi::v141-c-R007-C002","v141-c-R007::phi::v141-c-R007-C003"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R011::x::v141-c-R011-X-d","v141-c-R011::x::v141-c-R011-X-delta","v141-c-R011::phi::v141-c-R011-C002","v141-c-R011::phi::v141-c-R011-C003"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e009","v141-b-g02-e018","v141-b-g02-e020","v141-b-g02-e021"],"rationale":"The source explicitly states that the two clearing forms correspond through load reparameterization and preserve the physical quotas and the objective value; missing items in the frozen chain and the hub self-loop problem prevent unconditional closure."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-K003-J08","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R009","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R012","kind":"alternative_representation","from_refs":["v141-c-R009::phi::v141-c-R009-C003"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R012::phi::v141-c-R012-C002"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e010","v141-b-g02-e021","v141-b-g02-e024"],"rationale":"The direct per-node profit and the hub charge plus load-shifting remuneration correspond to the same consumer's total profit; applicability depends on the load correspondence stated by the source."}],"object_mappings":[{"mapping_id":"v142-d-K003-O01","kind":"same_node","member_refs":["v141-c-R006::V::bidding.demand","v141-c-R007::V::bidding.demand","v141-c-R010::V::bidding.demand","v141-c-R011::V::bidding.demand"],"canonical_ref":"v141-c-R007::V::bidding.demand","display_policy":"single_representative","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e038","v141-b-g02-e019","v141-b-g02-e021"],"rationale":"The ontology anchor of the same declaration function appears repeatedly; the representative selection does not eliminate the declaration representations and scopes of the two mechanisms."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-K003-O02","kind":"same_node","member_refs":["v141-c-R007::V::clearing.social_welfare","v141-c-R008::V::clearing.social_welfare","v141-c-R011::V::clearing.social_welfare"],"canonical_ref":"v141-c-R007::V::clearing.social_welfare","display_policy":"single_representative","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e009","v141-b-g02-e016","v141-b-g02-e020","v141-b-g02-e021"],"rationale":"Exhibits the same welfare-clearing function; the different mathematical representations and conditions each remain frozen."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-K003-O03","kind":"same_quantity","member_refs":["v141-c-R006::theta::v141-c-R006-T002","v141-c-R007::theta::v141-c-R007-theta-alphad","v141-c-R008::theta::param_alpha_d","v141-c-R009::theta::v141-c-R009-T002"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e038","v141-b-g02-e009","v141-b-g02-e010","v141-b-g02-e013"],"rationale":"The same M02 consumer quoted price is used respectively for the declaration, clearing, response, and settlement profit."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-K003-O04","kind":"same_quantity","member_refs":["v141-c-R006::theta::v141-c-R006-T001","v141-c-R007::theta::v141-c-R007-theta-bard","v141-c-R008::theta::param_dbar"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e038","v141-b-g02-e009","v141-b-g02-e013"],"rationale":"The same M02 total-request upper bound constrains the sum of the per-node loads."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-K003-O05","kind":"same_quantity","member_refs":["v141-c-R006::theta::v141-c-R006-T003","v141-c-R007::theta::v141-c-R007-theta-Nd"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e038","v141-b-g02-e009"],"rationale":"The delivery-node set declared in M02 enters the clearing index range."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-K003-O06","kind":"same_quantity","member_refs":["v141-c-R007::x::v141-c-R007-x-dn","v141-c-R008::x::var_d_n","v141-c-R009::x::v141-c-R009-X001"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e009","v141-b-g02-e010","v141-b-g02-e013","v141-b-g02-e015"],"rationale":"The meanings are all nodal load components of a single consumer; the index notation of the R008 formula is listed separately as a gap, and the original object is not rewritten."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-K003-O07","kind":"same_quantity","member_refs":["v141-c-R007::x::v141-c-R007-x-pi","v141-c-R008::x::var_p_i","v141-c-R009::x::v141-c-R009-X002"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e009","v141-b-g02-e014","v141-b-g02-e016"],"rationale":"The same M02 supplier injection is used for clearing, profit, and revenue reconciliation; the capacity-notation difference does not disappear with the quantity mapping."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-K003-O08","kind":"same_quantity","member_refs":["v141-c-R007::x::v141-c-R007-x-fk","v141-c-R008::x::var_f_k","v141-c-R009::x::v141-c-R009-X003"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e009","v141-b-g02-e014","v141-b-g02-e016"],"rationale":"The same M02 directional edge flow is used at different stages; whether the nonnegative domain is inherited still must be made explicit."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-K003-O09","kind":"same_quantity","member_refs":["v141-c-R007::x::v141-c-R007-x-theta","v141-c-R008::x::var_theta_n"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e009","v141-b-g02-e014"],"rationale":"The same M02 phase angle enters the clearing problem and the transmission profit problem, respectively."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-K003-O10","kind":"same_quantity","member_refs":["v141-c-R008::x::var_pi_n","v141-c-R009::theta::v141-c-R009-T001"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e009","v141-b-g02-e010","v141-b-g02-e016"],"rationale":"The same nodal clearing price is a variable in the coordination chain and an input parameter in the settlement chain; both roles are retained."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-K003-O11","kind":"same_quantity","member_refs":["v141-c-R010::theta::theta_bar_d","v141-c-R011::theta::v141-c-R011-T-bar-d","v141-c-R012::theta::v141-c-R012-theta-dbar"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e019","v141-b-g02-e020"],"rationale":"The same M03 hub requested quantity bounds the metering range of clearing and of settlement."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-K003-O12","kind":"same_quantity","member_refs":["v141-c-R010::theta::theta_alpha_d","v141-c-R011::theta::v141-c-R011-T-alpha-d","v141-c-R012::theta::v141-c-R012-theta-alpha-d"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e019","v141-b-g02-e020","v141-b-g02-e024"],"rationale":"The same M03 hub demand quoted price enters the clearing value and the consumer profit."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-K003-O13","kind":"same_quantity","member_refs":["v141-c-R011::x::v141-c-R011-X-d","v141-c-R012::x::v141-c-R012-x-d"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e020","v141-b-g02-e024"],"rationale":"The same total cleared load enters the hub profit term."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-K003-O14","kind":"alternative_representation","member_refs":["v141-c-R011::x::v141-c-R011-X-delta","v141-c-R012::x::v141-c-R012-x-delta"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e019","v141-b-g02-e020","v141-b-g02-e024"],"rationale":"Both denote hub load shifting, but the two chains differ in whether the index range includes the hub itself; a complete same-quantity identification is not made for the time being."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-K003-O15","kind":"alternative_representation","member_refs":["v141-c-R007::x::v141-c-R007-x-dn","v141-c-R011::x::v141-c-R011-X-d","v141-c-R011::x::v141-c-R011-X-delta"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e009","v141-b-g02-e020","v141-b-g02-e021"],"rationale":"The nodal load vector and the vector of total load plus load shifting belong to the reparameterization stated by the source and cannot be equated object by object; the self-loop condition remains to be resolved."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-K003-O16","kind":"alternative_representation","member_refs":["v141-c-R007::phi::v141-c-R007-C002","v141-c-R011::phi::v141-c-R011-C002"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e009","v141-b-g02-e020","v141-b-g02-e021"],"rationale":"The source says that the two forms have the same optimal objective value, but they use different load coordinates, and the frozen expression of R011 does not list the minimization operator, so they cannot be selected as the representative of one and the same expression."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-K003-O17","kind":"alternative_representation","member_refs":["v141-c-R009::phi::v141-c-R009-C003","v141-c-R012::phi::v141-c-R012-C002"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e010","v141-b-g02-e021","v141-b-g02-e024"],"rationale":"The two expressions correspond to different load coordinates and charge splits of the same consumer profit; applicability depends on the hub correspondence conditions that are not closed."}],"gaps":[{"gap_id":"v142-d-K003-G01","category":"upstream_missing","description":"R011 does not deliver the constraint objects for the (2.23b) nodal balance, the (2.23f) DC relation, and the (2.23g) capacity set, and it also lacks complete object interfaces for the phase angle and for the hub and node sets; C002 retains only the objective term and has no minimization operator.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R010","v141-c-R011","v141-c-R012"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R010::phi::v141-c-R010-C001","v141-c-R011::phi::v141-c-R011-C002","v141-c-R011::phi::v141-c-R011-C003","v141-c-R012::theta::v141-c-R012-theta-pi"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e019","v141-b-g02-e020"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"C completes, in an explicit subsequent revision, the clearing constraints and object interfaces already present in the source; this round does not use the alternative chain to cover these missing items."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-K003-G02","category":"ambiguous_mapping","description":"The nonnegative domain of load shifting in (2.23) excludes the hub itself, yet the summation includes the entire delivery-node set; R012 additionally includes that self-loop index. Whether the self-loop is absent or is fixed at zero is not made explicit, and this affects the bijection and the profit equivalence stated by the source.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R007","v141-c-R011","v141-c-R012"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R011::x::v141-c-R011-X-delta","v141-c-R011::phi::v141-c-R011-C003","v141-c-R012::x::v141-c-R012-x-delta","v141-c-R012::phi::v141-c-R012-C002"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e019","v141-b-g02-e020","v141-b-g02-e021","v141-b-g02-e024"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Check the self-loop definition and the summation range, and then make explicit the applicable domain of the load reparameterization."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-K003-G03","category":"ambiguous_mapping","description":"The supplier subproblem of R008 retains a capacity upper bound without a supplier subscript; on that basis, the parameter cannot be unconditionally identified as the element-wise upper bound of each supplier's capacity set.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R007","v141-c-R008"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R007::theta::v141-c-R007-theta-Cp","v141-c-R008::theta::param_pbar","v141-c-R008::phi::v141-c-R008-C003"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e009","v141-b-g02-e014","v141-b-g02-e015"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"B confirms the capacity subscript in (2.20b) and its relation to the clearing capacity set, and C then revises it explicitly."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-K003-G04","category":"ambiguous_mapping","description":"The R008 consumer objective uses j on the delivery-node set and the node mapping n(j), whereas R007 and R009 use the node index n; no explicit correspondence definition of the two indexings is currently given.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R007","v141-c-R008","v141-c-R009"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R008::phi::v141-c-R008-C002","v141-c-R009::phi::v141-c-R009-C003"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e009","v141-b-g02-e010","v141-b-g02-e013"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Check the node and consumer index conventions, keep the frozen formulas, and avoid treating a notational inference as a confirmed identity."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-K003-G05","category":"ambiguous_mapping","description":"Source (2.22) uses the sum of demand over the nodal consumer set; R009-C002 instead uses the single-consumer nodal load and sets to zero the nodes that are not provided. This equivalent translation still requires confirmation.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R007","v141-c-R009"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R007::phi::v141-c-R007-C003","v141-c-R009::phi::v141-c-R009-C002"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e009","v141-b-g02-e016"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"B clarifies the demand notation of (2.22), and C makes explicit the range used in the translation; no new charge variable is created."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-K003-G06","category":"math_incomplete","description":"The M02 chain does not explicitly restate the nonnegative domain of directional flow, whereas R011 of M03 records a real-valued flow domain; the DC constraint on the two-direction difference cannot by itself restrict the common directional component. In addition, the supplier sign in the expansion of source (2.17) is inconsistent with the balance in (2.16), and the complete dual derivation is not yet closed.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R007","v141-c-R008","v141-c-R009","v141-c-R011"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R007::x::v141-c-R007-x-fk","v141-c-R008::x::var_f_k","v141-c-R009::x::v141-c-R009-X003","v141-c-R011::x::v141-c-R011-X-f"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e009","v141-b-g02-e011","v141-b-g02-e012","v141-b-g02-e020"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Check the flow domain inherited by each mechanism and the signs in (2.17), and have C record them explicitly; constraints must not be silently filled in from other mechanisms."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-K003-G07","category":"ontology_extension","description":"The virtual link and the load-shifting service are still represented only through the cleared quantity and the payment function; the corresponding node proposal remains pending approval.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R006","v141-c-R007","v141-c-R008","v141-c-R009","v141-c-R010","v141-c-R011","v141-c-R012"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R011::x::v141-c-R011-X-delta","v141-c-R012::V::settlement.payment"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e018","v141-b-g02-e019","v141-b-g02-e024"],"proposal_ids":["v141-b-g02-p-virtual-link","v141-b-g02-p-load-shifting-service"],"required_work":"Manually assess the proposal and its direction and service semantics; this round does not add graph objects."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-K003-G08","category":"unverified_source","description":"The cross-mechanism equivalence statement, the profit expression, and the revenue reconciliation all come from B evidence that remains unverified; the experiment has not performed an independent source audit.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R006","v141-c-R007","v141-c-R008","v141-c-R009","v141-c-R010","v141-c-R011","v141-c-R012"],"object_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e038","v141-b-g02-e009","v141-b-g02-e010","v141-b-g02-e013","v141-b-g02-e014","v141-b-g02-e016","v141-b-g02-e019","v141-b-g02-e020","v141-b-g02-e021","v141-b-g02-e024"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Independently check the original text, the indices, the direction, and the reparameterization conditions; all mappings continue as candidates for manual inspection."}]},"rule_refs":["42-data_center_space_time_flexibility::v141-c-R006","42-data_center_space_time_flexibility::v141-c-R007","42-data_center_space_time_flexibility::v141-c-R008","42-data_center_space_time_flexibility::v141-c-R009","42-data_center_space_time_flexibility::v141-c-R010","42-data_center_space_time_flexibility::v141-c-R011","42-data_center_space_time_flexibility::v141-c-R012"],"unresolved_rule_refs":[],"node_ids":["COMP-29875534ea059f1d","COMP-851574b724899235","COMP-9d6b95c27c0765d4","COMP-ea3eb5ca8dc0c382","COMP-ebacec241379c91d","KG40-c62513665ebf8550"]});
